      "text": [
        "A Wyle Cop firm, built on referrals rather than adverts.",
        "Hale & Pryce was founded in 1987 by David Hale and Margaret Pryce, two Shrewsbury solicitors who believed clients deserved a fixed fee, a named point of contact, and a call back the same day. Nearly forty years on, those are still the rules the firm runs on.",
        "We're based a short walk from the Square, opposite the old Music Hall, and most of our new clients still come to us because a neighbour, colleague or family member sent them our way.",
        "A named solicitor, not a call centre",
        "You'll deal directly with the person handling your case, by phone or email, not a rotating case-handling team.",
        "Fixed fees wherever possible",
        "For conveyancing and standard wills, you'll know the total cost before we start work — no surprise invoices later.",
        "Local knowledge that speeds things up",
        "We know local agents, surveyors and the Shropshire Council land searches team, which often shaves days off a transaction.",
        "Regulated and insured",
        "Authorised and regulated by the Solicitors Regulation Authority, with full professional indemnity cover.",
